# The API is on its own hostname, served by IIS on a different machine, so this
# must be the absolute https URL. There is no proxy on admin.everfresh.ae: a
# relative /api/v1 would resolve against the panel's own host, miss every file,
# and fall through nginx's SPA rewrite - so each API call would return
# index.html with a 200. The app reads that as a logged-out session and there
# is nothing in the console to explain it.
#
# Safe despite being cross-origin. Browsers judge first- vs third-party by
# registrable domain, and admin.everfresh.ae and api.everfresh.ae share
# everfresh.ae, so the refresh cookie is same-site and no browser blocks it.
# It does mean CORS applies: the backend's ALLOWED_ORIGINS has to contain
# https://admin.everfresh.ae with that exact scheme, and COOKIE_DOMAIN has to
# be .everfresh.ae for the cookie to be accepted on this hostname at all.
#
# Every VITE_* value is inlined into the public JS bundle at build time, so
# this is build configuration, not a secret. These files are tracked on
# purpose: ignored, a server build found no env file and silently fell back to
# the default in src/lib/constants.ts, where a wrong URL and a missing one look
# identical.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.everfresh.ae/api/v1
VITE_APP_NAME=Everfresh Admin
VITE_APP_VERSION=1.0.0
